Adds the asset at `path`.

The asset can be `Cow::Borrowed(&'static [u8])` for static bytes, `Cow::Owned(Vec<u8>)` for
bytes you already have, or a closure that returns them on demand (see [`FnAssetLoader`]).

# Errors

Returns [`DuplicateAssetPath`] if `path` is already registered. The existing entry is kept.

# Examples

```
# use gpui::*;
# use std::borrow::Cow;
let mut assets = AssetRegistry::default();
assets
    .insert(
        "icons/star.svg",
        Cow::Borrowed(
            &b"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 8 8\"><rect width=\"8\" height=\"8\"/></svg>"[..],
        ),
    )
    .unwrap();

assert!(assets.load("icons/star.svg").is_some());
assert!(assets.load("icons/missing.svg").is_none());
assert!(assets.insert("icons/star.svg", Cow::Borrowed(&b""[..])).is_err());
```

Returns a guard that calls `f` with `entity` when the guard is dropped.

`f` doesn't run if the entity has been released by then. Hold the guard in a
variable. A guard that is dropped at once runs `f` immediately.

# Examples

```
use gpui::{AppContext, TestApp};

let mut app = TestApp::new();
let log = app.update(|cx| cx.new(|_| Vec::<&'static str>::new()));
let guard = app.update(|cx| {
    cx.to_async().on_drop(&log.downgrade(), |log, cx| {
        log.push("finished");
        cx.notify();
    })
});
drop(guard);
app.read(|cx| assert_eq!(*log.read(cx), vec!["finished"]));
```
